# Test: data-import-existing
# VALIDATES: AC-9 -- with ze stopped, `ze data import <file>` naming a config that already has an active version (left by the first start) prints `imported file/active/<name> (<n> bytes)` and `1 files imported into <store>`, commits the file as a new active version and keeps the previous one as rollback; the daemon started next from the store serves the imported peer and router-id 2.2.2.2.
# PREVENTS: an offline import that writes only the file/active mirror, which the active pointer shadows, so the next start runs the old config while the import reported success.
# QUESTION: does a daemon started from the store after an offline import run the imported config? TestDataImportReplacesThroughAVersion reads the store; only a real start shows which config the daemon resolves and applies.
#
# The second start is a bare `ze start`: it binds the store as the config
# source (cmd/ze/ze_core_start.go, cmdStart, ConfigSourceStored) and boots the
# name resolve.DefaultConfig answers for a store with no instance name,
# ze.conf, from its active version. A start naming the file binds the FILE as
# the authority (ConfigSourceFile), and cmd/ze/hub/config_source.go
# initializeConfigSource rebuilds the store from it at boot, overwriting the
# import: that is the file mode working as designed, not the path AC-9 asks
# about. The file ze.conf stays in place with the boot router-id 1.2.3.4, so a
# daemon serving 2.2.2.2 can only have read the store.

option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=90s

tmpfs=ze.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
    authentication {
        user admin {
            password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
        }
    }
}

environment {
    ssh {
        enabled true
        server main {
            ip 127.0.0.1;
            port $PORT2;
        }
    }
}

bgp {
    router-id 1.2.3.4
    session {
        asn {
            local 65000
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

# The first start, from the file, creates the store and its first active version of ze.conf.
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start ze.conf:name=first:ready=Ze running.
cmd=stop:seq=2:name=first:signal=term
# With ze stopped, the offline import replaces that config.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=le test fixture storage/data-import-existing-seed:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: data-import-existing-seed
# The next start takes its config from the store and must run what the import committed.
cmd=background:seq=4:exec=ze start:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=le test fixture storage/data-import-existing $PORT2:exit=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: data-import-existing
cmd=stop:seq=6:name=daemon:signal=term
